Error: Jet.SingleUseDropped: `t` still owes `join` or `detach`
  --> Tests/UI/unjoined_task.jet:2:5
    |
  2 |     t: task 42
    |     ^
 Why: This value's type is `#SingleUse`, so it carries a job that has to be done — dropping it without doing that job leaves the work undone (an unjoined task, an unreleased lock)
 Fix: Consume it exactly once: call `.join()` or `.detach()` on it, pass it to a `^^` parameter, or `return` it — or write `#Unsafe("reason") { consume(t) }` to discard it deliberately
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.SingleUseDropped
